\f1\b0 \cb3 \'a0But it is essentially a- a tweak to make the model larger without consuming more compute in each forward pass. So there is this fully connected layer, and if listeners are familiar with multi-layer perceptrons, you can think of a mini multi-layer perceptron, a fully connected neural network layer inside the transformer. And it\'92s very expensive, because it\'92s fully connected. If you have a thousand inputs, a thousand outputs, that\'92s like a one million connections. And it\'92s a very expensive part in this transformer. And the idea is to kind of expand that into multiple feedforward net- uh, networks. So instead of having one, let\'92s say you have 256, but it would make it way more expensive, because now you have 256, but you don\'92t use all of them at the same time.\
