\f1\b0 \cb3 \'a0So you now have a router that says, \'93Okay, based on this input token, it would be useful to use this fully connected network.\'94 And in that context, it\'92s called an expert. So a Mixture of Experts means you have multiple experts. And depending on what your input is let\'92s say it\'92s more math-heavy, it would use different experts, compared to, let\'92s say, translating input text from English to Spanish. It would maybe consult different experts. It\'92s not quite clear, I mean, not as clear-cut to say, \'93Okay, this is only an expert for math and for Spanish.\'94 It\'92s a bit more fuzzy. But the idea is essentially that you pack more knowledge into the network, but not all the knowledge is used all the time.\
