\f1\b0 \cf5 \cb3 \ul \ulc5 \strokec5 (01:58:32)}}
\f1\b0 \cb3 \'a0So I would personally start, like you said implementing a simple model from scratch that you can run on your computer. The goal is not if you built a model from scratch to have like something you use every day for your personal projects. Like it\'92s not going to be your personal assistant replacing an existing open weight model or ChatGPT. It\'92s to see what exactly goes into the LLM, what exactly comes out of the LLM, how the pre-training works in that sense on your own computer preferably. And then you learn about the pre-training, the supervised fine-tuning, the attention mechanism.\
