\f1\b0 \cb3 \'a0You get a solid understanding of how things work, but at some point you will reach a limit because more models can only do so much and the problem with learning about LLMs at scale is I would say it\'92s exponentially more complex to make a larger model because it\'92s not that the model just becomes larger. You have to now think about sharding your parameters across multiple GPUs. Even for the KV-cache, there are multiple ways you can implement it. One is just to understand how it works, just to grow the cache. There\'92s like a cache you grow step by step by let\'92s say concatenating lists on growing it, but then that wouldn\'92t be optimal in GPUs. You wouldn\'92t do that. You would pre-allocate a tensor and then fill it in. But that adds again another 20, 30 line- lines of code.\
