{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://youtube.com/watch?v=EV7WhVT270Q&t=8949"}}{\fldrslt 
\f1\b0 \cf5 \cb3 \ul \ulc5 \strokec5 (02:29:09)}}
\f1\b0 \cb3 \'a0So, different kinds of approaches than the current LMs?\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Sebastian Raschka\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://youtube.com/watch?v=EV7WhVT270Q&t=8953"}}{\fldrslt 
\f1\b0 \cf5 \cb3 \ul \ulc5 \strokec5 (02:29:13)}}
\f1\b0 \cb3 \'a0Yeah, so we talked a lot about the transformer architecture and the autoregressive transformer architecture, specifically, like GPT. And it doesn\'92t mean no one else is working on anything else . So, people are always on the, let\'92s say, lookout for the next big thing. Because I think it would be almost, like yeah, stupid not to. Because sure, right now, the transformer architecture is the thing, and it works best and there\'92s, right now, nothing else out there. But, you know, it\'92s always a good idea to not put all your eggs into one basket. So, people are developing other things alternatives to the autoregressive transformer. One of them would be, for example, text diffusion models.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Sebastian Raschka\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://youtube.com/watch?v=EV7WhVT270Q&t=8989"}}{\fldrslt 
\f1\b0 \cf5 \cb3 \ul \ulc5 \strokec5 (02:29:49)}}
\f1\b0 \cb3 \'a0And listeners may know diffusion models from the image generation, like Stable Diffusion popularized it. There was, like, a paper on generating images. Back then, people used GANs, Generative Adversarial Networks. And then there was this diffusion process where you iteratively de-noise an image, and that r- resulted in really good quality images over time. Stable Diffusion was a company. Other companies build their own diffusion models. And then people are now like, \'93Okay, can we try this also for text?\'94 Doesn\'92t, you know, make intuitive sense yet, because it feels like, okay it\'92s not something continuous like a pixel that we can differentiate. It\'92s, like, a discrete text, so how do we implement that de-noising process?\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Sebastian Raschka\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://youtube.com/watch?v=EV7WhVT270Q&t=9025"}}{\fldrslt 
\f1\b0 \cf5 \cb3 \ul \ulc5 \strokec5 (02:30:25)}}
\f1\b0 \cb3 \'a0But i- it\'92s kind of, like, similar to the BERT models by Google. Like, when you go back to the original transformer, and so they were, like, the encoder and the decoder. The decoder is what we are using right now in, in GPT and so forth. The encoder, i- it\'92s more like a parallel, let\'92s say, technique where you have multiple tokens that you fill in in parallel instead of\'85 So, GPT models, they do autoregressive one token at a time. You, you complete the sentence one token at a time. And in BERT models, you have a text that\'92s a sentence that has gaps. You, like, mask them out. And then one iteration is filling in these gaps.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Sebastian Raschka\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://youtube.com/watch?v=EV7WhVT270Q&t=9062"}}{\fldrslt 
\f1\b0 \cf5 \cb3 \ul \ulc5 \strokec5 (02:31:02)}}
\f1\b0 \cb3 \'a0And text diffusion is kind of like that, where you are starting with, let\'92s say, some random text, and then you are filling in the missing parts or you\'92re refining them iteratively, and you have multiple iterations. And the cool thing here is that this can do multiple tokens at the same time. So, it\'92s kind of, like, the promise of having it more efficient. Now, the, the trade-off is, of course, well, how good is the quality? It might be faster. And then now you have this dimension of the de-noising process. The more steps you do, the better the text becomes. And people, you know\'85 I mean, you, you can scale in different ways. They try to see if that is maybe a valid alternative to the autoregressive model in terms of giving you the same quality for less compute.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Sebastian Raschka\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://youtube.com/watch?v=EV7WhVT270Q&t=9106"}}{\fldrslt 
\f1\b0 \cf5 \cb3 \ul \ulc5 \strokec5 (02:31:46)}}
\f1\b0 \cb3 \'a0Right now, I think it\'92s\'85 You know, there are papers that suggest, okay, if you want to get the same quality, you have to crank up the de-noising steps and then you end up spending the same compute you would spend on an autoregressive model. The other downside is, well, it\'92s parallel, which sounds appealing, but some tasks are not parallel. Like, you know, like, reasoning tasks, tool use, maybe where you have to ask an in- code interpreter to give you an intermediate result, and that is kind of tricky with diffusion models. So, there are some hybrids. But, yeah, the main idea is how can we parallelize it. And so interesting avenue. I think right now, there are mostly research let\'92s say, models out there, like LaMDA and some other ones.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Sebastian Raschka\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://youtube.com/watch?v=EV7WhVT270Q&t=9144"}}{\fldrslt 
\f1\b0 \cf5 \cb3 \ul \ulc5 \strokec5 (02:32:24)}}
\f1\b0 \cb3 \'a0I, I saw some by startups, some deployed models. There is no big diffusion model at scale yet. Like, you know, like, Gemini, ChatGPT scale, l- on that level. But there was an announcement by Google or, like, a, a site where they said they are launching Gemini Diffusion, and they put it into context of their, I think, Nano2 model, and then they said basically for the same quality on most benchmarks, we can generate things much faster. So, you mentioned what\'92s next. I don\'92t think the text diffusion model is going to replace autoregressive LLMs, but it will be something maybe for quick cheap at scale tasks. Maybe the free tier in future will be something like that.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

