\f1\b0 \cf5 \cb3 \ul \ulc5 \strokec5 (02:33:04)}}
\f1\b0 \cb3 \'a0Mm-hmm. I think there\'92s a couple examples where it\'92s\'85 I, I\'92ve heard that it\'92s actually been started to be used. I think to paint an example of why this is so much better, for example, when GPT-5 is taking 30 minutes to respond, it\'92s generating one token at a time. And this diffusion idea is essentially generate all of those completion, all of those tokens and the completion in one batch, which is why it could be way faster. And I think it could be suited-\'85\
