\f1\b0 \cb3 \'a0the startups I\'92m hearing are, like, code s- startups where you have a code base, and you have somebody that\'92s effectively vibe coding, and they say, \'93Make this change.\'94 And a code diff is essentially a huge reply from the model, but it doesn\'92t have to have that much external context, and you can get it really fast by using these diffusion models. So that\'92s what I\'92ve heard of one example is that they use these text diffusion to generate really long diffs because doing it with a autoregressive model would take minutes, and that time for, like, a user-facing product causes a lot of churn. So, like, every second, you lose a lot of users.\
