\f1\b0 \cb3 \'a0The problem is you can\'92t just do that for each person because it would be too expensive to update the weights for each person, and, and I think that\'92s the problem. So unless you get\'85 I th- I mean, even at OpenAI scale, building the data centers, it would be too expensive. I think that is only feasible once you have something on the device where the cost is on the consumer. Like what Apple tried to do with the Apple Foundation models, putting them on the phone, and then they learn from the experience.\
