\f1\b0 \cb3 \'a0So we\'92ve, like, gotten to pretty quickly to, like, a million tokens of input context length. And I would expect it to keep increasing and, like, get to, like, 2 million or 5 million this year, but I don\'92t expect it to go to, like, 100 million. That would be like a true breakthrough, and I think those breakthroughs are possible. Like, the continual learning thing I think of it as a research problem where you could\'85 there could be a breakthrough that just makes transformers work way better at this and it\'92s cheap. Like, these things could happen with so much scientific attention. But turning the crank, it\'92ll be s- consistent, m- m- increases over time.\
