\f1\b0 \cb3 \'a0I think also looking at the extremes, I think there\'92s, again, no free lunch. So, well, the one extreme to make it cheap, you have a, let\'92s say an RNN that has a single spa- uh, state where you save everything from the previous stuff. It\'92s like a specific fixed size thing so you never really\'85\'85 grow the memory because it\'92s \'85 You are stuffing everything into one state, but then the longer the context gets, the more information you forget because you ca- you can\'92t keep \'85 I mean, compress everything into one state. Then on the other hand, you have the transformers, which try to remember every token, which is great sometimes if you want to look up specific information, but very expensive because you have the KV cache that grows, the dot product that grows.\
